#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""sixi-speech: speech recognition and speech synthesis next to the Sixi-ASI Engine, on the CPU.

The engine uses the GPU for the language model; speech runs on CPU cores so that it does not slow the answers
down. The service speaks the OpenAI audio API, so one client covers text, images and speech:

  POST /v1/audio/transcriptions   multipart form: file=<audio>, optional language=en|de|..., model=whisper, response_format=json|text
                                  language=pl|de|it|fr with audio of up to 2 s: a short answer ("nie", "ja") is heard in that
                                  language and not as English (lead_in=0 in the form turns this off for one request;
                                  certain=1 returns a text only when it was heard the same way twice, else nothing)
  POST /v1/audio/speech           JSON: {"input": "...", "voice": "pl", "response_format": "wav"|"pcm"|"mp3"|..., "speed": 1.0}
                                  "deterministic": true (or "noise_scale": 0, "noise_scale_w": 0): the same audio every time
  GET  /v1/models, GET /health

Commands:

  sixi-speech setup                 an isolated Python environment under ~/.sixi/speech, the runtime, the models
  sixi-speech link                  put this command on the PATH (~/.local/bin)
  sixi-speech serve                 the service in the foreground (http://127.0.0.1:8088)
  sixi-speech service install       as a systemd user service; then start | stop | restart | status | logs | remove
  sixi-speech say "Dzien dobry" --voice pl -o out.wav
  sixi-speech transcribe file.wav

Recognition: NVIDIA Parakeet TDT 0.6b v3 (25 European languages, among them English, German, Italian, French and
Polish; it detects the language); Whisper turbo for other languages (language=zh) or on request (model=whisper).
Parakeet has no input for the language, and a word of one syllable is too little for it to tell: with
language=pl, de, it or fr the service hears a clip of up to 2 s together with a phrase in that language, spoken
by its own voice (once in front of the clip, once behind it), and takes the phrase off the text again. Give the
language whenever you know it. Where a wrong word is worse than no answer, add certain=1.
Synthesis: Piper voices, one per language: en, de, it, fr, pl, pl-female (or the name of a voice folder). Both run
through sherpa-onnx on the CPU.

The log (stdout; ~/.sixi/speech/service.log for the systemd service) has one line per request with the audio
length, the time taken, the model or voice and the number of characters. It holds no recognised or spoken text
unless the service is started with --log-text (or SIXI_SPEECH_LOG_TEXT=1), which is meant for debugging only.
"""
